# src/Verifier.sol is generated verbatim by snarkjs from the proving key. Its
# identifiers, visibility keywords and inline assembly are not ours to change,
# and the next circuit build would undo any edit. It is already excluded from
# forge fmt and forge lint (the `ignore` entries in foundry.toml) and from the
# coverage gate (`coverage-exclusions` in .github/workflows/ci.yml); this is the
# same carve-out for the same reason, kept at the site rather than in the shared
# config, because a shared config naming a path that exists in only some repos is
# a rule about somebody else's tree.
#
# PF-S123 ruled that both of the estate's generated verifiers stay
# generated-and-UNMODIFIED — no Ownable, no edits of any kind — so their source
# keeps matching the bytecode verified on Basescan. Here that also avoids a
# cascade: ZKComplianceRegistry holds the verifier address as an `immutable`, so
# touching the verifier would force the registry and KYCToken to redeploy with it.
src/Verifier.sol
